        <mxCell id="n22" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" value="FINDING G1 (High, VERIFIED). manual_add_booking sends a NAIVE datetime. (a) It is stored into a timestamptz column via the server&#39;s local tz — a 10:00 walk-in came back as 07:30 IST on this box; on a UTC server it would read 15:30. Every manual service booking shows the wrong time on My Day and the slip. (b) has_calendar_conflict then compares naive vs tz-aware and raises TypeError → 500 on the 2nd overlapping booking. The existing test hides this by reusing one session; a fresh session reproduces the crash." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="360" x="1198" y="700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e23" edge="1" parent="1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#b85450;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="n22" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="1378" y="530" as="sourcePoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n24" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" value="FINDING G2 (Med). The Add form hardcodes every name as section=&#39;pair&#39;, status=&#39;living&#39;, and service purpose as &#39;khushali_nu&#39;. A manually-added Patet machi records its DEPARTED pair as &#39;living&#39;; farmayeshne and real purpose are never captured. Doc 07 says closed-vocab fields (purpose) must be selectable — here purpose isn&#39;t even offered." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="340" x="819" y="700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n26" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" value="Multi-agyari: My Day merges all agyaries (good); Machi Board is per-agyari via the switcher. But the switcher only lists ALREADY-joined agyaries — no &#39;join another&#39; action (see Finding D1, Flow 2)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="300" x="998" y="82" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e27" edge="1" parent="1" source="n2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#d6b656;exitX=1;exitY=0.3;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.3;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="n26" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
